@startuml
title Tuna -> ISP -> Store Controller (POS) Host Sync

autonumber
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAF7
skinparam sequence {
	ArrowColor #2D5B87
	LifeLineBorderColor #2D5B87
	LifeLineBackgroundColor #F1F6FB
	ParticipantBorderColor #355E3B
	ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF6EE
	ParticipantFontColor #1F2A1F
}

actor "Tech/Process" as Tech
participant "TUNA" as TUNA
participant "ISP" as ISP
participant "Store Controller\n(POS)" as POS

note over TUNA,POS
Scope is small at a basic-operations level, but host sync is the most complex path
because ISP performs most transformation and orchestration steps.
end note

== Initial Sync Payload ==
Tech -> TUNA: Makes changes in TUNA
TUNA -> TUNA: Tuna update process triggers\nPOS host file update process
TUNA -> ISP: Copy hosts, resolv, and bootptab
note right of ISP
bootptab is generated from /ha/dhcptab for ISP script compatibility.
end note

== ISP Processing Loop ==
loop Repeat while new LANE assignments are discovered
	ISP -> ISP: Receive hosts, resolv, bootptab
	ISP -> POS: Push resolv file
	ISP -> POS: Pull hosts file
	ISP -> ISP: Extract LANE assignments and adxautonet entries

	alt New LANE assignments found
		ISP -> TUNA: Send new LANE data
		TUNA -> TUNA: Rebuild hosts file with new LANEs
		TUNA -> ISP: Send updated hosts/resolv/bootptab
	else No new LANE assignments
		ISP -> ISP: Continue processing
	end
end

== Final Host File Transformation ==
ISP -> ISP: Remove xx and DHCP entries from hosts
ISP -> ISP: Add MAC addresses as comments
ISP -> ISP: Reinsert adxautonet entries
ISP -> POS: Deliver final host file

note over ISP,POS
Final result: POS receives resolved resolv and transformed host file.
end note

@enduml

